===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Related to the Sunni branch of [[Islam]].
#* {{quote-book| author=H. E. Wingate| year=1919| title=Records of Iraq, 1914-1966| volume=2| page=181| books.google.com/books?isbn=1852078200| editor=Alan de Lacy Rush, Jane Priestland year=2001| passage=I therefore strongly advocate the formation of a local capital but not at Hillah, which is too '''Sunni''' and near Baghdad}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Discourse and the Construction of Society| page=36| books.google.com/books?isbn=0195079094| author=Bruce Lincoln| year=1992| passage=members {{...}} came to view themselves collectively as the righteous descendants of Husayn confronting an evil and fundamentally alien ruler: a shah more Zoroastrian than Muslim, more '''Sunni''' than Shi'i, more Arab than Iranian, more Yazid than Husayn.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Religion And Politics In Turkey| page=124| books.google.com/books?isbn=0415348315| author=Alİ Çarkoğlu, Barry M. Rubin| year=2005| passage=When we compare the data in these registers with findings presented above, in fact, Sivas appears more "'''Sunni'''" than the Balkan-Anatolian average of 1695.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Iraq’s New Political Map| page=16| books.google.com/books?isbn=142231006X| passage=After the formation of Tawafuq and under the impetus of growing Sunni extremism, it became more '''Sunni''' in orientation.| year=2007}}
#* {{quote-book|title=No End in Sight: Iraq's Descent Into Chaos| page=357| books.google.com/books?isbn=158648608X| author=Charles H. Ferguson| year=2008| passage=Omar is a very '''Sunni''' name. Although some Shiites name [their sons] Omar, but not to the extent we say it's a Shiite name. It's a very '''Sunni''' name in the Islamic history.}}
#* {{quote-book| title=The Strong Horse: Power, Politics, and the Clash of Arab Civilizations| page=41| books.google.com/books?isbn=0385532202| author=Lee Smith| year=2010| passage=In keeping with the status-anxietyridden logic of the convert, many of the minorities became more '''Sunni''' than the Sunnis themselves}}
#* {{quote-book| title=The Making of Terrorism in Pakistan: Historical and social roots ...| page=98| books.google.com/books?isbn=1135169411| author=Eamon Murphy| year=2012| passage=Many Shias who had become more '''Sunni''' in their religious practices reverted back to their original sect.}}

